{"2894540": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Ex Libris", "steam_appid": 2894540, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Midway through the journey of your life, you have found yourself at the gates of the legendary Abbey of St. Theleme, a monastery of great learning and of great mystery. </i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2894540/extras/8de268a26b0ba0a8fffcbcc6b477df41.avif?t=1783093346\" width=468 height=569 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Ex Libris</i></strong> is a library-crawling RPG adventure set in a 16th century  monastery, inspired by the writings of Umberto Eco, Francois Rabelais, and Clark Ashton Smith. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Built using FromSoft's Sword of Moonlight RPG toolkit (based on the King's Field engine), <strong><i>Ex Libris</i></strong> is a unique retro literary adventure. Explore the monastery and its ruins, learn ancient tongues, uncover lost texts, and unravel the strange threads that bind the obscure history of Theleme and its inhabitants, including yourself. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >10+ hours of non-linear exploration-based RPG gameplay</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hundreds of in-game texts to read, including both obscure real-world texts and  new writing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two ancient languages (Ancient Greek and Latin) to learn along with a new conlang, Old Occident </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Midway through the journey of your life, you have found yourself at the gates of the legendary Abbey of St. Theleme, a monastery of great learning and of great mystery. </i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2894540/extras/8de268a26b0ba0a8fffcbcc6b477df41.avif?t=1783093346\" width=468 height=569 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Ex Libris</i></strong> is a library-crawling RPG adventure set in a 16th century  monastery, inspired by the writings of Umberto Eco, Francois Rabelais, and Clark Ashton Smith. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Built using FromSoft's Sword of Moonlight RPG toolkit (based on the King's Field engine), <strong><i>Ex Libris</i></strong> is a unique retro literary adventure. Explore the monastery and its ruins, learn ancient tongues, uncover lost texts, and unravel the strange threads that bind the obscure history of Theleme and its inhabitants, including yourself. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >10+ hours of non-linear exploration-based RPG gameplay</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hundreds of in-game texts to read, including both obscure real-world texts and  new writing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Two ancient languages (Ancient Greek and Latin) to learn along with a new conlang, Old Occident </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul>", "short_description": "Ex Libris is a library-crawling RPG adventure set in a 16th century monastery, inspired by the writings of Umberto Eco, Francois Rabelais, and Clark Ashton Smith. ", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2894540/514b49979c1d984f91fdd155e20395161e26d182/header.jpg?t=1783093346", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2894540/b6032c9608c215cbfabd724136ba6d7f409dc743/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1783